## 1. The Big Idea

_Three families, one parent, one shared floor. Every compound — Test, Masteron, Tren, all of them — bolts onto the **same muscle-output baseline** (you build roughly the same lean tissue). What rises **above** that floor is different for every family: water, estrogen, progestogen, suppression, organ strain. The poster makes "which steroid is strongest?" visibly the wrong question, and replaces it with "which bill, and have I earned the climb?"_ It is a reference chart a reader studies to place any compound at a glance and predict its behaviour before looking it up — not a motivational image, and not a menu to shop from.

## 2. Visual Metaphor & Structure

A **derivation / parts-genealogy tree drawn over a shared OUTPUT DATUM** — the visual language of an engineering part-lineage chart (a base part number spawning variant SKUs, each with a logged deviation from parent) fused with a single horizontal baseline that every variant lands on. The metaphor earns its place four ways:

1. **The article is literally a lineage.** Testosterone is the root; DHT (via 5α-reduction) and Nandrolone (via 19-demethylation) are *derived* from it. A derivation tree with labelled transform-valves on each branch is the honest shape of the argument — and it's a sub-archetype the Fit set has never used.
2. **The shared OUTPUT DATUM draws the myth-buster for free.** A single horizontal rail — `NITROGEN RETAINED ≈ 60–75 g LBM/day` — that *every* compound chip connects down to at the **same height** is the chemical proof that the muscle built is comparable. The eye sees "all equal at the floor" instantly.
3. **The divergence draws itself above the line.** Each compound carries a small **side-effect signature plume** rising above the datum (water / aromatization / progestogenic / suppression / dryness). Same floor, different plumes = "same destination, different journey" as literal geometry. No caption needed.
4. **The tree IS the ladder.** Read bottom→top, the three families stack in the exact learning-and-derivation order (Test root → DHT → 19-nor crown), so "climb one at a time, exhaust before ascending" is the reading direction itself.

The compound chips are **engineering part cards** (part name · family tag · base/anchor badge if applicable · the one-line signature). The **misfits** are part cards physically sitting in the wrong rack with a cross-coloured tag and a thin cross-link arrow pointing to the family they actually behave like. The **19-nor crown** carries the single red interlock (the suppression latch). A quiet **family→pathway bridge** in the footer ties this map back to 3.0's console.

This is a deliberately *different instrument* from the prior PE posters but lives in the same locked "Engineering Diagnostic Instrument" language — and it is the natural visual sibling to 3.0: 3.0 was the mechanism map (console), 3.1 is the lineage map (derivation tree), and they share the "two maps of the same territory" framing.

