## 5. UX / visual encoding expectations _(semantic — colors come from design.md, not from here)_

- **The shared OUTPUT DATUM is the load-bearing object.** It must be the boldest horizontal element on the poster, and every compound chip must visibly connect to it at the *same* height. If a reader takes only the datum and three lanes, they should still get "same muscle, different cost." Protect its prominence above all chrome.
- **The divergence is vertical, above the line; the equality is the line itself.** Encode the side-effect cost as plume *height/density* above the datum (taller/denser = more baggage), so 19-nor reads as the busiest plume and DHT as the cleanest — without needing to read a word. Use position + height, not just hue, so it survives grayscale.
- **Red is rationed to exactly ONE object: the 19-nor suppression interlock.** It is the only true danger in the article (irreversible-feeling, months-long shutdown, the Part-1 commitment made concrete). Everything else cautionary — the progestogenic/prolactin note, the misfit flags — stays in the **amber/caution** role or neutral instrument ink. (Consistent with the whole PE set: ~1 red object, reserved for the one real failure.)
- **The misfits must look misfiled.** A Halotestin card physically sitting in the Test lane but wearing a DHT-coloured tag, with a thin cross-link arrow to the DHT lane, is the teaching device. Make the cross-tag and the arrow unmistakable so "the family is a default, not a law" reads pre-attentively. Three misfits, three cross-links — no more.
- **The BASE / ANCHOR badge is a distinct, repeated glyph.** It appears on exactly four cards (Test, Dbol, Boldenone, MENT) and nowhere else, so "only these can anchor a cycle" is a visual fact, not buried prose.
- **The climb is the layout.** Bottom→top must read as Test → DHT → 19-nor. The numbered climb-order rail and the rising tree should agree; the red crown sits at the *top* of the climb so the reader cannot reach it without passing the lower rungs.
- **Hierarchy of attention:** headline → the shared OUTPUT DATUM + three lanes (hero) → the divergent plumes → the misfit cross-links → the red suppression crown → the climb-order rail and footer bridge (quiet chrome). Within each lane: the family name + signature loudest, the part cards supporting, the misfit flag a deliberate interruption.
- **Restraint = the mood.** A precision lineage chart, not a poster of drug names. Dark instrument ground, mono part-labels and tick-marks, ruler-drawn branch lines and the datum rail, generous negative space between lanes. Color rationed to the plumes (cost), the one red crown (danger), and the base-badge accent.
- **Saveability:** shape/position carry the meaning (datum height, plume height, lane order, badge glyph, cross-link arrows) so the chart parses on a phone and in grayscale — a reader should still see "all equal at the floor, different above, climbed in order" with color stripped.

